# Python bytecode caches
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# warden evidence run dirs (uploaded as CI artifacts, never committed)
.warden/out/

# review-memory derived cache — rebuilt by `warden memory ingest` from the
# committed shards in .warden/memory/attest/; committing it conflicts on
# every concurrent branch
.warden/memory/findings.jsonl

# gate shards — local working state, re-derived by the next `warden review`.
# The DoD's mutation proof (plant a pattern, watch the gate fire, revert)
# writes these, so committing one files a synthetic defect against a commit
# no ref contains. Rung R-11 fails Level 3 if any are tracked.
.warden/memory/gate/
